# PlayThing fstab. Block device names are the partition names (docs/boot.md).
# /system is system_b, the stock B slot.
# /data is not in this file: init mounts it in post-fs with data-setup.sh
# (docs/persistent-data.md): an ext4 image file on the stock "data" partition, or ext4 on
# zram1 (RAM) if a check fails. Not tmpfs: PackageManager needs the "user.serial" xattr on
# user directories, and tmpfs on Linux 4.9 has no user.* xattrs. Not in fstab, because a
# failed /data mount in mount_all makes init reboot to recovery.
#<src>                <mnt_point>   <type>   <mnt_flags>                                       <fs_mgr_flags>
/dev/block/system_b   /system       ext4     ro,barrier=1                                      wait
/dev/block/zram0      none          swap     defaults                                          zramsize=134217728
